     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Zafirlukast:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " competitive inhibitor of leukotrienes D4 and E4. Zileuton: inhibits 5-lipoxygenase."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " oral long-term control in mild to severe persistent asthma; not for an acute attack. Montelukast: weigh neuropsychiatric risk first, especially when symptoms are mild and other therapies work."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Montelukast (≥ 15 y) 10 mg once daily in the evening. Zafirlukast (≥ 12 y) 20 mg twice daily, ≥ 1 h before or 2 h after meals. Zileuton 600 mg four times daily (2400 mg/day)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Montelukast boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " serious neuropsychiatric events (agitation, aggression, depression, sleep disturbance, suicidal thoughts/behavior). Liver enzyme elevation (mainly zileuton); zafirlukast: life-threatening hepatic failure reported. Rare EGPA (Churg-Strauss)-like syndrome, sometimes as oral steroids are reduced."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Zafirlukast:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " contraindicated in hepatic impairment, including cirrhosis. Zileuton: contraindicated in active liver disease or transaminases ≥ 3× ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Zileuton roughly doubles theophylline levels (reduce theophylline, monitor levels), raises PT with warfarin, and doubles propranolol exposure. Zafirlukast raises S-warfarin exposure and PT (~35%); erythromycin lowers zafirlukast levels (~40%)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Zileuton:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ALT before starting, monthly × 3 months, every two to three months for the rest of the first year, then periodically; stop if liver symptoms or transaminases > 5× ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Montelukast:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " watch for behavior/mood changes; stop and call the prescriber if new neuropsychiatric symptoms or suicidal thoughts occur. Keep a SABA for rescue."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
